gui-input-log 2
platform macos
window 480 320 2
source synthesized, not recorded: a two-finger flick on a macOS trackpad and its momentum, as AppKit sends it (NSEvent scrollWheel: phase MayBegin, then Began and Changed with precise scrollingDeltaY in points while the fingers move, Ended with no delta at the lift, then momentumPhase Began, Changed and Ended, with phase None), its phases as the window reads them off the NSEvent (gui-display's scroll phases: MayBegin and Began are began, Ended ended, momentumPhase Began, Changed and Ended are momentum-began, momentum and momentum-ended), its delta as winit 0.30 gives it (PixelDelta in logical points). The finger phase is sampled every 8-9 ms (a trackpad's report rate as AppKit coalesces it), the momentum every 16.7 ms decaying by 0.998 a millisecond (UIScrollView.DecelerationRate.normal, the system's documented deceleration) until under half a point; deltas are made up within those rules. A click lands on the list during the momentum.
